# Keep secrets, local data, test evidence and version control state out of every
# image. Docker sends this whole context to the daemon before building, so an
# entry missing here is a file shipped inside an image.
#
# Docker matches each pattern against the path relative to the context root, so
# a bare directory name only excludes that name at the root: `node_modules/`
# does not exclude `frontend/node_modules/`. Nested paths therefore use the
# `**/` prefix, which matches at any depth.
.git
.github
.atl
**/.env
**/.env.*
finance.db
finance.db-journal
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.xlsx
**/*.csv
verify/
odd/
openspec/
docs/
backend/tests/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/coverage/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
Dockerfile*
compose*.yaml
